BRepCheck: in parallel mode (BRepCheck_Analyzer's theIsParallel)
BRepCheck_Analyzer checks the faces on several threads, and each face checks
its edges in its context (BRepCheck_Edge::InContext), so an edge is checked
in the contexts of its two faces at the same time. Both compared the curves
on the faces with the edge's one curve adaptor (myHCurve, made by
Minimum()), and an adaptor of a B-spline curve caches the span it evaluated
last: one thread could evaluate the curve with the span another thread had
just cached and find the edge off its face (BRepCheck_InvalidCurveOnSurface),
which made the face unorientable (BRepCheck_UnorientableShape). A valid shape
then came out valid or invalid from run to run (the cut of a round groove
swept along a helix from a nut, mitcad#203). Each context now evaluates its
own copy of the adaptor (ShallowCopy(), as GeomLib_CheckCurveOnSurface does
for its threads); the sequential mode is unchanged, and so are the checks
and their statuses.
